test, and lint as turbo run build, turbo run test, turbo run lint.\n3. The scaffold files are committed to the existing git repository with git commands exiting 0.\n\nVERIFIED STATE (from the orchestrator, confirmed with git/node — trust these facts, but you may re-verify read-only):\n- Root package.json EXISTS and is committed (commit 6cc5d66, message \"chore: add root package.json with npm workspaces, npm@10, Node 22 engines, turbo 2.x, and turbo-run scripts\"). Working tree is clean for it. Its exact content:\n  {\n    \"name\": \"nextmove\",\n    \"private\": true,\n    \"workspaces\": [\"apps/*\"],\n    \"packageManager\": \"npm@10\",\n    \"engines\": { \"node\": \"22.x\" },\n    \"devDependencies\": { \"turbo\": \"^2.5.0\" },\n    \"scripts\": {\n      \"build\": \"turbo run build\",\n      \"test\": \"turbo run test\",\n      \"lint\": \"turbo run lint\"\n    }\n  }\n- Unit test file test/package.test.cjs is committed and PASSES 4/4 via `node --test test/package.test.cjs`. Tests map 1:1 to the ACs (AC1 fields, AC2 turbo devDep + scripts, JSON validity, etc.).\n- Completion marker .story-updates/STORY-setup-001a.passed is tracked in HEAD but DELETED from the working tree (git status shows ` D`). It must be recreated and committed.\n- Untracked harness files that must NOT be committed: .last-branch, .ralph/, .story-updates/processed/, prd.json.bak, ralph-summary.txt, ralph.log.\n- Known constraint: `npm test` (= `turbo run test`) FAILS because turbo 2.x rejects the literal packageManager value \"npm@10\" (its parser regex requires full semver, e.g. npm@10.8.2). The AC mandates the literal value npm@10, so the field must stay \"npm@10\" — the AC is the source of truth over turbo's runtime preference. The Test Strategy Gate classifies this story as pure scaffold → a sample passing unit test (which is green) is the required test; E2E not required.\n- No apps/ directory, no turbo.json, no .npmrc — none are required by the AC (the AC only requires the workspaces de